# Abstract
p = doc.add_paragraph()
p.add_run('Abstract - ').bold = True
p.add_run('The construction domain has an inherent randomness and danger associated with it that makes the automation of labor control extremely challenging [13]. Traditionally, computer vision systems applied in civil engineering have tried to amalgamate two inherently contradictory aspects of operation, namely the biometric recognition of workers and the verification of occupational safety standards (Personal Protective Equipment or PPE) [1]. Nevertheless, empirical and theoretical findings show that compulsory use of PPE such as safety helmets, dust masks, tinted glasses, and chin straps basically obstructs facial features, resulting in ineffective deep facial recognition systems and unsupportable rejection queues during shift changeovers [7]. This extensive literature review analyzes recent developments in deep learning-based object detection, access control systems, and finance automation technologies to overcome this operational challenge [17]. We analyze and critically assess: (1) the current best-in-class one-shot object detection algorithms (including YOLOv5, YOLOv8, attention-enabled backbones, and GhostNet lightweights) designed for small objects with heavy occlusions (PPE detection) [3]; (2) biometric and non-biometric digital identity solutions (including Facial Recognition, RFID, dynamic QR codes, and Virtual Kiosk architectures) [6]; (3) the empirical case for the Decoupled System Architecture with an explicit separation between deterministic identity verification at entry checkpoints and asynchronous computer vision monitoring of active work areas [11]; and (4) subsequent enterprise-level integrations, particularly automated payroll accounting, smart contracts, and wage disbursement engines [18]. Significantly, the synthesis we provide proves that, although the technology for attendance tracking and PPE detection has matured independently from an algorithmic perspective, there is a significant research gap concerning the implementation of such technology in an end-to-end fashion in which deterministic digital identity coupled with verified safety logs leads to automated payroll processes free from any disputes [14].')

# Keywords
