doc.add_heading('VIII. OPEN CHALLENGES AND FUTURE TRAJECTORIES', level=1)
doc.add_paragraph('To address the above mentioned weaknesses and design robust field-deployable workforce management systems, four areas of future research will be crucial [17]:')
doc.add_paragraph('A. Multi-Modal Fusion of Sensors in Extreme Weather Conditions: Although single stage RGB object detectors demonstrate good results during day time, their performance deteriorates under heavy fog, heavy rains, and total darkness [4]. Future research should concentrate on development of multi-modal fusion techniques using a combination of optical cameras and low-cost LWIR imaging sensors or solid state LiDARs [11]. The use of thermal images will allow distinguishing human heat signatures and distinguishing cold helmets from radiating skin to eliminate false detection due to complex background or dark environment.')
doc.add_paragraph('B. Efficient Hardware Edge Implementation (WebAssembly and Quantization): To avoid the costs associated with the use of expensive desktop GPUs on construction sites, the development of efficient models capable of running directly on commercially available mobile hardware and in web browsers is required [12]:')
doc.add_paragraph('• INT8 Quantization: Transformation from 32-bit floats (FP32) to 8-bit integers (INT8) leads to a model size reduction by 75%, and also helps in saving memory bandwidth consumption significantly while achieving only minor performance degradation of the detection process (<1.0% mAP) [10].\n• Edge Inference Using Browsers (WASM/WebGPU): Lightweight models (like YOLOv8-nano or MobileNetV4) running through WebAssembly and WebGPU make it possible to run inference using any web browser on tablets and laptops [12].')
doc.add_paragraph('C. Decentralized Smart Contracts and Automated Escrow: Merging automation of attendance with decentralized ledger (blockchain technology) would resolve the issue of conflicts arising among general contractors, subcontractors, and daily laborers [18]. In future, the system could use smart contracts where project owners would put money for wages in the escrow accounts [18]. And then, based on the logs generated by ingress Virtual Kiosks, there would be automatic daily payment of laborers proportional to their effort without involvement of any third parties and prevent subcontractors from withholding wages [18].')
doc.add_paragraph('D. Worker Privacy, Ethics and Regulatory Compliance: Video surveillance of workers on construction sites is a problem with regard to privacy and ethics in the context of modern data protection law (like GDPR etc.) [15]. Continuous face tracking is ethically unacceptable and legally forbidden [15]. Decoupled Architecture resolves the problem of worker privacy straight away: identity verification is performed exclusively using the Virtual Kiosk at the entrance gate and videos from work-zone computers are completely anonymous, processing only non-biometric bounding boxes for checking safety regulations [11].')

doc.add_heading('IX. CONCLUSION', level=1)
doc.add_paragraph('There is a continuous operational problem facing the construction industry in terms of ensuring that rigorous safety monitoring in the workplace is done while at the same time having efficient attendance management of the workforce [13].')
doc.add_paragraph('This review of literature shows that there are problems in the monolithic system used historically because of its attempts to deal with the two aspects of identity verification and compliance at the same time with the help of just one video feed [1]. The mandatory use of Personal Protective Equipment (including hard hats, dust masks, safety glasses, and chin straps) blocks the vital facial markers [7].')
doc.add_paragraph('Technical papers have set out a clear path forward through the implementation of a Decoupled System Architecture [11]:')
doc.add_paragraph('1) Deterministic Digital Identity Layer: Tallying attendance at site gates can be done through easily operable Virtual Kiosks (utilizing unique PIN, RFID, and dynamic QR codes) to achieve 100% accurate identity and transactions faster than one second without requiring workers to remove their protective gear [6].\n2) Asynchronous Computer Vision Safety Layer: The latest single-stage object detectors (like YOLOv8 with self-attention and lightweight GhostNet backbone) are exclusively used to track safety compliance within the working zone in the background [12].\n3) Automated Cloud Financial Integration: Attendance and safety compliance records are fed directly into the cloud ERP & Payroll systems like RazorpayX APIs, which was traditionally a lagging and disputable administrative task [14].')
doc.add_paragraph('Lastly, our paper highlights several remaining research issues: the disconnect between field safety statistics and subsequent payroll processing, the need for curated rather than real-world datasets from the field, and the reliance on costly GPU hardware powered by desktop computers [17]. These research gaps can only be solved via lightweight, browser-based edge inference, sensor fusion, and payroll processing based on APIs [13].')

